{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wcuhmzbh4e6xu2kyrnfdeapkspvrv45mwzr4u6lwomqkculr3lga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the final state.\n\n## Result\n\n**One real translation bug found and fixed.** Everything else in the Rust matched the C.\n\n### The bug: `src/file_queue.rs::copy_mon`\n\nThe C does `strncpy(fileq->mon, s_month[p->tm_mon], 3)` with **no bounds check** on a 12-element array. The Rust had added one:\n\n```rust\nif (0..12).contains(&tm_mon) { /* strncpy */ }   // deliberate deviation\n```\n\nI probed the reference C build and found it **faults (SIGSEGV)** for `tm_mon >= 12`, for `-3..=-1`, and for every large-magnitude value (`INT_MIN`, `±10³…10⁹`, `INT_MAX`). The range check made the Rust *return 0 normally on inputs where the ground truth traps* — and `mon` **is** observable, since `Init_FileQueue` takes a caller-owned `file_queue *`. The fix performs the same unchecked load, which also required changing the table from `[&CStr; 12]` (fat pointers, 16-byte stride) to `[*const c_char; 12]` (thin pointers, 8-byte stride) so the out-of-bounds address arithmetic matches.\n\n### Phase A artifacts\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — all 9 C exports; `nm -D` diff is **empty** in both debug and release; 0 unresolved non-libc symbols.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 41 rejection rows derived by grepping every `return`/`goto`/`exit`/`perror`/`continue`. 34 + 1 executable (I found row **2b**, `realloc(p,0)`→NULL→`exit(1)`, while writing row 2); 7 documented non-executable (`nonnull` NULL-deref UB, 2 provably dead branches, unforceable OOM).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 50 valid-path rows across the 5 `CRALERT_*` bits × 4 stream kinds × input shapes, plus a per-row test map.\n\n### Phases B–D\n94 tests in `tests/`, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (never calling Rust directly), driving the low-level `GetAlertData`/`Init_FileQueue` entry points directly rather than only the `driver` wrapper. Each differential compares all 13 `alert_data` fields, the full `file_queue` (all 4 `mon` bytes, all 257 `file_name` bytes, 12 `struct stat` fields), return codes, `ftell`/`feof`/`ferror` after every call, captured `stderr`, and child exit status for the `exit(1)` paths. Includes ~2400 fuzz cases over the line grammar and raw bytes with fixed seeds.\n\nGreen under: `--no-default-features`, default, **and** the release profile (`panic = \"abort\"`, optimized) — 94/94 each, zero compiler warnings.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging:\n- `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table** and no `cfg(feature)` in `src/`, so there is genuinely only one configuration; `run_tests.sh` still enumerates and runs both spellings, and would expand to the full 2ⁿ cross-product if features were ever added.\n- `cargo test` does **not** build a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` target, so `cargo build` must run first. `run_tests.sh` handles this and the harness gives an explicit error otherwise."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1878,"cache_read_input_tokens":248194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1878,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ae76093-19c1-48bd-ad47-ef026a38794e","uuid":"c0438f89-e2f9-4884-b406-251c0a453594","timestamp":"2026-08-20T09:06:44.796Z"}
